      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 the authors 0270-6474/17/370464-10$15.00/0.",
        "AbstractText": "It is possible that one of the essential functions of sleep is to take out the garbage, as it were, erasing and \"forgetting\" information built up throughout the day that would clutter the synaptic network that defines us. It may also be that this cleanup function of sleep is a general principle of neuroscience, applicable to every creature with a nervous system."
      },
